description: No comments; keep code clean, lean, and deduplicated
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code quality

- Never add code comments: no `//`, `/* */`, JSDoc/`/** */`, or JSX `{/* */}`. Do not leave commented-out code. Generated files (e.g. `next-env.d.ts`) are exempt.
- Prefer clear names and structure over explaining code in prose.
- After substantive edits, remove dead code, unused exports/deps, duplicate helpers, and leftover scaffolding.
- Prefer shared utils over copy-paste (`lib/`, shared components). Extend existing helpers before adding parallel ones.
- Keep diffs focused: no drive-by refactors unrelated to the task. Update docs when behavior changes (`docs-sync.mdc`); do not add unsolicited extra markdown.
- Prefer simple, readable implementations; avoid unnecessary abstraction, memoization, or “clever” patterns unless already established in the repo.
- Do not inflate UI for accessibility theater (e.g. forcing large min-heights on every text link). Keep touch targets on real controls; keep layout compact.
